sommelier: don't make new surfaces enter an output on their first commit

On the first commit of a surface with a role, sommelier sends
wl_surface.enter for the internal output if the host hasn't sent one, a
workaround for Chrome, which didn't track which output a surface is on.
For an xdg_toplevel that commit is the initial one, without a buffer,
before the first configure.

GTK takes the enter as a scale change, and Firefox recomputes its bounds
from its window, still at GTK's placeholder size. That size replaces the
one Firefox restored from its last session, so Firefox opens at its
minimum size, 500x200, every time.

Host compositors like Mutter and KWin send wl_surface.enter themselves
once the surface is on an output, and sl_surface_enter forwards it. Drop
the workaround.

